    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the maximum possible number of planes that can be formed by 12 points in space, we need to consider that any three non-collinear points uniquely determine a plane. Therefore, we calculate the number of ways to choose 3 points from 12 points, and this will give us the number of unique planes.\n\nThe formula to find the number of ways to choose 3 points from 12 points is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{r} \\), which represents the number of ways to choose \\( r \\) elements from a set of \\( n \\) elements without regard to the order of selection. In this case, we need to find \\( \\binom{12}{3} \\).\n\nLet's calculate this using Python and then provide the answer.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the number of ways to choose 3 points from 12 points\nn = 12\nr = 3\nnumber_of_planes = math.comb(n, r)\nprint(number_of_planes)\n```\n```output\n220\n```\nThe maximum possible number of planes that can be determined by 12 points in space is \\(\\boxed{220}\\).",
