      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine how many different planes can be formed by selecting 3 points from the given 12 points.\n\nThe formula to calculate the number of combinations of n items taken k at a time is:\n\nC(n, k) = n! / [k! * (n-k)!]\n\nwhere \"!\" denotes factorial.\n\nIn this case, we want to select 3 points at a time from 12 points, so we have:\n\nC(12, 3) = 12! / [3! * (12-3)!]\n       = 12! / [3! * 9!]\n       = (12 * 11 * 10) / (3 * 2 * 1)\n       = 220\n\nThus, the maximum possible number of planes that can be determined by 12 points in space is 220.",
